# ============================================================================
# 06_ Build ASPC and fibroblast-stroma signatures — v9 ADAPTIVE FILTERS
# ============================================================================
#
# SELECTION HIERARCHY
#
#   Fibroblast-stroma signature
#     Full DOWN candidate matrix
#       | Apply adaptive filters using Adeno tau, ratio, and correlation
#       |   requirements (tier ladder relaxes until the target can be met)
#     Eligible fibroblast candidates
#       | Rank by descending evidence_score
#       | Select up to cfg$target_size genes
#     Final fibroblast-stroma signature
#
#   ASPC signature
#     Full UP candidate matrix
#       | Exclude genes selected in the fibroblast-stroma signature
#       | Apply adaptive filters using NEPC tau, ratio, and correlation
#       |   requirements (tier ladder relaxes until the target can be met)
#     Eligible ASPC candidates
#       | Force AR inclusion if necessary, replacing the lowest-ranked
#       |   ordinary selected gene when the signature is full
#       | Rank by descending evidence_score
#       | Select up to cfg$target_size genes
#     Final ASPC signature
#
# ADAPTIVE FILTERS
#   - Each branch walks a tier ladder from strict to loose. The first tier that
#     yields at least cfg$target_size eligible genes is used. If no tier does,
#     the tier with the most eligible genes is used and a shortfall is reported.
#   - Every tier requires a finite branch tau >= tier tau and a finite branch
#     ratio >= tier ratio (never below cfg$tau_floor / cfg$ratio_floor).
#   - Correlation requirements are direction-specific:
#       ASPC (UP):        cor_NEPC >= cor_NEPC_min  and cor_AR <= cor_AR_max
#       Fibroblast (DOWN): cor_NEPC <= cor_NEPC_down_max and cor_AR >= cor_AR_down_min
#     Late tiers drop the correlation gates and finally allow missing
#     correlations; the tier reached is written to the diagnostics.
#   - Filters decide ELIGIBILITY; evidence_score decides MEMBERSHIP.
#
# FORCED INCLUSION
#   - cfg$aspc_forced_genes (default "AR") are guaranteed membership in the
#     ASPC signature when they are measured in bulk and not already taken by
#     the fibroblast-stroma signature. A forced gene bypasses the adaptive
#     filters. When the signature is already full, the lowest-ranked
#     ordinary (non-forced) selected gene is displaced.
#   - Forced genes are flagged (forced_inclusion = TRUE) and displaced genes
#     are recorded (selection_status = "displaced_by_forced_gene").
#
# WHAT IS RETAINED FROM v8
#   - Existing evidence and annotation weights and evidence_score.
#   - Branch-specific tau and atlas support.
#   - Imported elastic-net, stability, and WGCNA flags.
#   - CSPA surface annotations, cache, and explicit fallback.
#   - TNFSF12 and MDK ligand annotation overrides.
#   - Unweighted mean gene-wise z-score for bulk signature scoring.
#   - Ranked files with explicit rank and selection information.
#
# INTERPRETATION
#   - evidence_score is a manually weighted prioritization score.
#   - Annotation membership is not proof of ASPC identity.
#   - The tier reached determines how strong the specificity claim is: a
#     signature built at a tier without correlation gates should be described
#     as "top N by evidence among genes with tau >= X", not as "genes with
#     high cell-type specificity".
#   - Missing evidence contributes zero points, not proof of biological absence.
#   - Zero-score genes may be selected if needed to fill the requested size.
#   - The input bulk values are used as supplied. No library-size normalization
#     or log transformation is introduced by this script.
#
# IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
#   Partial correlations are calculated using base-R QR residualization of BOTH
#   gene expression and ASPC_fraction against the same usable covariates.
#   They are unavailable if the fraction/covariates or residual variation are
#   insufficient. They feed the score only; the adaptive filters use the
#   unadjusted cor_NEPC and cor_AR trait correlations.
# ============================================================================

